# Rows sql_alert_transitions() skips: a host id, a rule's hash or a transition id that is no blob of 16 bytes.
# C tests them in that order and counts a row once, at the first that fails; one record per call has the three
# counts. A window's host list holds only real ids, so a bad host id shows by the transition's id alone; a bad
# transition id by a window alone; a bad hash (the alarm's and its rule's, equal) by both.
database real
